  progressiveHintRules:
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_GlutinousRice_Ratio
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Glutinous rice should use the Large amount. It is the base of this recipe.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_BlackSesame_Ratio
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Black sesame should use the Medium amount, just below glutinous rice.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_RedBean_Ratio
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Red bean should use the Small amount.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_LotusLeaf_Ratio
    priority: 19
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Lotus leaf should use the Very Small amount. It is light and easy to cover.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_Main_Batch_Combination
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Red bean, glutinous rice, and black sesame should be ground together in the first batch.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_Lotus_Separate_Combination
    priority: 19
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Lotus leaf should be ground last in its own separate batch.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_RedBean_Order
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Red bean should go first. It builds the base.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_LotusLeaf_Order
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Lotus leaf should be last, after the first three ingredients have formed the main batch.
  - ruleId: L09_Hint_Middle_Order
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Start with red bean, glutinous rice, and black sesame together. Add lotus leaf last in its own batch.
